 one@clinet.fi (Tero Valkonen) writes:
 
> This subject probably has been recently discussed
> here but since I think here is a major
> disadvantage to the player I think the dev team
> should fix it. [Slow monster follows up stairs,
> gets in first hit, kills character.] If this isn't
> unfair then what is? The same goes for monsters
> who throw weapons at you. They can move, pick up a
> dart (for example) and throw it at you in the same
> round! This oughta be fixed, too!

That one doesn't irritate me nearly as much as having
monsters who blunder around the room swatting at
shadows when they are trying to hit my invisible
character somehow develop infallible aim as soon as
they change from swinging things to throwing things.

> PS. There's one silly thing about military
> barracks; whenever you are stealthy, the soldiers
> sleep. I think in every barrack there should be at
> least one guard who cried alert if the player
> enters the room the soldiers are in. Sleeping
> soldiers are too easy to kill.

Not just soldiers. I walked into my first ever
special beehive room (pretty damned impressive,
maybe 50 killer bees in one room), and _every_
_single_ bee stayed asleep until I hit it. The
result, at my then armor class, dexterity, and
experience level was a slaughter, in the wrong
direction. Normally, that room should have been
instant death for my character, or at least forced
me to seek the shelter of a door to keep from
fighting eight bees at once, rather than a walkover.

I know the dev team sort of got sick of the whole
thing at 3.0h, but there's lots in nethack that
still needs cleaning up, and it would be so nice
to have one robust version of the code that isn't
doing panics and stupid stuff for a change; I'd
rather have a good 3.0z than a buggy 3.1a.

Too much to wish for?

